lerting).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mentoring</strong> engineers on technical approach across both architecture and AI/agentic best practices, raising the team's execution level over time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evaluating</strong> and incorporating both internal (Nubank) and external AI tools and agents into our workflows, based on what best fits our needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnering</strong> with Nubank's central AI/platform teams and other BUs to share learnings and stay aligned on tooling direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enabling </strong>more Nubankers to safely contribute to AI-powered products over time (engineers and non-engineers)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Embedding</strong> responsible, auditable practices in everything shipped, across platform and AI systems alike, per applicable regulations and internal risk standards.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a person who has</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven technical leadership as a senior/staff engineer delivering high-impact, large-scale software systems in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of mentoring and uplifting peers on technical approach and AI-native workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong systems/platform engineering experience: architecture, CI/CD, test automation, able to evolve infrastructure to support reliable adoption of new technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine interest and foundational knowledge of AI/LLM concepts, ready to build hands-on fluency with our agentic tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership mindset for rolling out AI/agentic tooling across a team, driving adoption of testing, CI/CD validation, and evaluation practices, not just personal use.<