 - Research regulations and project management for its implementation.

 - Project management related to new regulations and licensing processes.

 - Lead efforts and align requirements towards new financial licenses.

 - Evaluate from a compliance perspective new products and features to be launched.

 - Keep other teams abreast of requirements by researching regulatory and filing information; writing and communicating guidelines.

 - Provide advisory to other teams about the regulation to establish new processes or controls.

 - Monitor and respond to inquiries received from Regulators, Auto Regulatory bodies or Auditors.

 - Create and update Compliance policies and procedures.

 - Liaise and work closely with various teams to enhance systems and processes related to Compliance.

 - Coordinate or support regulatory reviews or audits.

 - Support in identifying regulatory gaps and tracking its implementation.

We believe in

 - Entrepreneurship spirit;

 - Exceptional team chemistry;

 - Ownership

How We Work

 - You act like you own the company where you work

 - You are enthusiastic about building partnership with other teams

 - You are willing to go the extra mile and getting involved in many areas

 - You challenge the status quo

 - You thrive in dynamic, fast-paced, results-oriented teams

 - You are hungry and enjoy being constantly challenged to learn and do more



Requirements

 - +7 years' or above experience in regulatory compliance,  AML or regulatory areas for Banks, SOFIPO and/or Fintechs.

 - Proven experience in filing and obtention of financial licenses such as Fintech or Bank and project management for that.

 - Experience with CNBV & Banxico regulatory requirements for Financial Institutions.

 - Ability to develop policies and procedures from scratch and implement them.

 - Ability to conduct regulatory advisory and law interpretation by providing consultation to business areas as well as internal clients.

 - Ability to tackle complex problems involving several topics/variables, such as business, regulatory, finance and product.

 - Ability to work and lead through influence multidisciplinary teams (product, software engineering, data science, analysts and customer service).

 - Self-starter and ability to work independently.

 - Great team player, communication (written and verbal) and listening skills.

 - Fluency in both English and Spanish.

The position is based in Mexico City, Mexico

Work model

[Hybrid / On-Site]

Office requirement

2 days per week at the office.

 


